Hi,

I have an AlphaStation 255 on which I'm running NetBSD 2.0.2 as a 
headless server. It's a nice machine but periodically it either reboots 
itself or drops into DDB. Nothing in /var/log/messages suggests a 
problem, it just seems to happen spontaneously. I guess it's a kernel 
panic but then savecore doesn't yield anything on reboot. The machine 
does not run under a heavy load and is connected to a UPS.

I was wondering if this is a known problem at all or if it's something 
specific to my machine. It occurred to me that it might be firmware 
related for some reason. Any thoughts, please?


Thanks,

Jeff



